<title>USA: Aluminum orders rise 6.7 pct in July - Spector.</title>
<headline>Aluminum orders rise 6.7 pct in July - Spector.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. aluminum orders in June rose 6.7 percent over July 1996, with can sheet orders up 9.3 percent in the same time frame, industry analyst Stewart Spector said.</p>
<p>&quot;The year-to-year comparisons of bookings this month and next could be flat to up modestly,&quot; Spector said. &quot;Last year bookings in August and September rebounded, but then quickly declined when LME ingot price fell to new lows last October and November.</p>
<p>&quot;However, in the last three weeks LME prices have risen quite rapidly, so later this month end-users might do some price hedging buying for next year.&quot;</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1646))</p>
